{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792865081,"nonce":"xfTsq2Jtlsy/bpn3cCxtU2HKwyw=","title":"TypeScript: typed ambient function declarations","message":"About 67 official rows stopped at a declare function signature. A declare function is now typed like any other signature and never lowered: argument errors at its calls are reported as TypeScript reports them, a declaration without a return type is TypeScript's 7010, and the call itself, or the function used as a value, reports Unsupported, since its body lies outside the program (external linking stays a gap, as for ambient variables).","files":null}]}